  "limits": [
    "Step bounds the number of forward attempts, not wall time. A large prefill chunk still occupies the backend until that attempt returns; no kernel preemption or per-call latency bound is promised.",
    "Interleaving is caller-serialized, each forward still belongs to one session. No multi-request matrix batching, overlapping GPU execution, dynamic serving admission, network server or throughput/tail latency parity claim.",
    "The standalone qualification harness runs fixed two-session cohorts; it is an artifact under /tmp, not a new benchmark CLI mode or production scheduler. Public resumable API and orchestration tests are in the repository.",
    "Real weights cover two related multilingual prompts and five generated tokens. Interleave schedules are AB committed and BA prediction-first (also under ASAN/GPU tools); this is not the full order-by-mode cross product or broad model/domain/long-decode coverage.",
    "BUSY/cancel/failure behavior is exhaustively exercised by orchestration stubs; real GPU interleave traces separately report whether BUSY actually occurred. Real GPU cancellation during a partial BUSY forward is not qualified here.",
    "No new performance capture. Prior fixed/sequential cache measurements belong to their recorded runtime hashes and cannot establish current vLLM parity.",
    "AVX2/AVX512 standard and CUDA compatibility suites passed on this host; no fresh ARM/Metal execution claim. Full modern-model/backends/offload/serving objective remains incomplete."
  ],
